{
  "slug": "audit-project",
  "name": "Audit Project",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Multi-agent iterative code review until zero issues remain. Spawns up to 10 specialist reviewers (code quality, security, performance, test coverage, architecture, database, API, frontend, backend, DevOps) chosen based on the project's signals. Each pass produces certainty-graded findings (HIGH / MEDIUM / LOW); HIGH findings auto-fix where safe. The orchestrator iterates passes until zero open issues remain or a max-iteration cap is reached. Specialists are role-based (defined inline via Task tool, not file-based agents) so they don't bloat the plugin's agent count. Designed to plug into /next-task and /prepare-delivery as the deep-review phase.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill** and **3 commands**.\n\n- **Skills** (1): `audit-project` (Use when user asks to 'review my code', 'audit the codebase', 'run code review', 'check for issues', 'find…)\n- **Commands** (3): `audit-project-agents` (Use when coordinating multi-agent review passes in /audit-project), `audit-project-github`, `audit-project` (Multi-agent code review with iterative improvement)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install audit-project@claude-community` from `agent-sh/audit-project`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 1,
    "command": 3
  },
